Z||000000||grinthock||05-30-2001||06:42 PM||||My door handles are VERY loose, I would love to make them tighter, makes the car FEEL cheap.  Anyone have any ideas about the common reason they get loose and giggly ?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://grinthock.2y.net/pics/87gt/S_P000386.JPG">  <P>Home page: <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com<BR>Home" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroworld.com<BR>Home</A>  of the fiero voting booth!<BR>Owner of 85 GT<BR>87 GT Silver<BR>1995 Ford Escort Wagoon POS||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||05-30-2001||06:46 PM||||There is a return spring that pulls the handle down.  They very often break loose of their mountings. Little tabs are bent over to hold the spring and these tabs break off. The tabs are made of pot metal and do not bend with out breaking. I have been unable to fix them and just replace the door handle assembly.  <P><P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||05-30-2001||07:03 PM||||Mine used to be jingly too.  Joe fixed one side but I never got around to doing the other.  He didn't replace it though.  Not sure what he did, I wasn't there at the time.  One side feels brand new, the other feels like it'll fall off!<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gangster.gif"> ||||reg||1
